## Nepali Cultural Occasion Terms

Use these naturally in copy, meta descriptions, and OG content. Never force-insert them.

| Term | Context |
|---|---|
| Dashain | Nepal's biggest festival — gifting time (October) |
| Tihar | Festival of lights — gifting, celebration (October/November) |
| Teej | Women's festival — personal gifts |
| Wedding | `विवाह` — custom figurines, nameplates, keepsakes |
| Anniversary | Relationship milestone — custom photos, pieces |
| Remembrance | Memory of a loved one — emotionally powerful context |
| Graduation | Academic milestone — personalised gift |
| Baby shower | New arrival — custom keepsakes |
| हाम्रो | "Our" in Nepali — part of the brand name, emotional resonance |

## Devanagari Copy Standards

- Always use Unicode Devanagari — never romanized Nepali for production content
- The brand name in Devanagari: `हाम्रो 3D`
- Devanagari content in templates: wrap in `<span lang="ne">हाम्रो 3D</span>`
- Devanagari headlines: use `font-h3d-devanagari` (Rozha One)
- Devanagari body: use `font-h3d-devanagari-body` (Noto Sans Devanagari)

## What NOT to Write

These patterns are banned from all Hamro3D copy:

- Superlatives: `Best`, `Cheapest`, `Fastest`, `#1`
- Sales language: `Limited time offer`, `Only X left`, `Flash sale`, `Discount`
- Generic e-commerce: `Shop now`, `Add to cart`, `Browse our store`
- Clinical descriptions: `High-quality PLA material`, `FDM technology`, `Layer resolution`
- Feature-first framing: `Supports 10 colors`, `Ships in 3–5 days`

Instead, lead with meaning:
- Not `High-quality PLA material` → `Crafted to last a lifetime`
- Not `Ships in 3–5 days` → `Delivered within 3–5 days of completion`
- Not `10 color options` → `Choose the finish that feels right`
